## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design a scalable, tenant-isolated CDC and schema evolution pipeline with robust governance, security, and rollback requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Change Data Capture (CDC) at cloud scale
- Per-tenant data isolation and architecture
- Schema drift detection and automated validation
- Backward-compatible migration strategies
- Data Catalog contract enforcement
- DLP-based PII masking and data protection
- Data Exchange for secure partner publishing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-logic: drift detection
function driftCheck(incomingSchema, currentSchema) {
  const changes = schemaDiff(incomingSchema, currentSchema);

  if (isBackwardCompatible(changes)) {
    generateMigration(changes);
    createSnapshot();
    applyMigration(changes);
  } else {
    alertSchemaViolation(changes);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesss ability to design scalable, privacy-preserving streaming pipelines with per-tenant controls and lineage. It also tests cross-region delivery and data-exchange mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped masking and schema versioning
- Streaming ingestion: Pub/Sub + Dataflow
- Per-tenant partitioned analytics in BigQuery
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog; sharing via Data Exchange
- 24h per-tenant rollback using raw logs in Cloud Storage

